<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Stormy Weather" spTempo="72">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1933
Composer:	Harold Arlen
Lyricist:	Ted Koehler
Form:	34-bar AABA (32-bar AABA with a two-bar extension before the bridge)
Style:	Torch song / jazz ballad
Key:	G major

Written for the 1933 Cotton Club revue, “Stormy Weather”
was first performed by Ethel Waters and became closely
associated with her, Lena Horne, and later jazz vocalists
and instrumentalists. The song’s melancholy lyric reflects
the end of a romance, while its extended AABA design
includes two extra bars before the bridge.</spComments>
